From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Scott Smith <scott@newtrostudios.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 18:35:06 -0400
Subject: remotesmith(0303): LAN-first route for saved peers, 3 s bound

DEC-11, DEF-8, AC-7, AC-8, AC-38. Upstream reaches a peer by ID only
through hbbs (its intranet path needs hbbs as well) and uses the direct
port 21118 only when the user types an IP, so with the VM down an ID
connect fails even on the home LAN.

Client::_start now tries the peer's LAN address(es) first: the address
that last worked (peer option remotesmith-lan-hint), LAN discovery's
IPs for that ID, and the address hbbs reports when it marks the peer as
local. All candidates race; the first that connects AND proves the saved
peer's ID in the identity handshake wins and the rest are dropped, so at
most one session results. Connect plus handshake share a 3 s budget,
then the ID route runs as before. Another machine at a stale address
fails the handshake (no password is ever sent) and the ID route takes
over; the same ID with a different key wins the race and is stopped by
the 0301 identity gate. Skipped under forced relay, a SOCKS proxy or the
WebSocket transport. The route shows as "LAN".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
